5x - 1 &= -3x - 2 \\
5x + 3x &= -2 + 1 \\
8x &= -1 \\
x &= -\frac{1}{8}
\end{aligned}
\]

The solutions are \(x = \frac{3}{2}\) and \(x = -\frac{1}{8}\). The smallest value among these is \(-\frac{1}{8}\).

Thus, the smallest value of \(x\) is \(\boxed{-\frac{1}{8}}\).

